# Every claim whose edge or narrowing is filed as an identity's output, beside whether that identity
# computes the claim. One row per such derivation, `violates` where the identity does not compute
# the claim's own position.
#
# A claim's edge is the edge of the terms that compute it
#   `boundOrigin` filed as a derivation says the bound was not set by anybody: the claim is an
#   identity's output, and its edge is the edge of that identity's terms. `narrowsWhen` filed as one
#   says the claim narrows as those terms do. Both are true only of the identity that computes the
#   claim: a share's edge can be `sharesSum`'s, a patience's cannot, because no identity computes a
#   patience. The two sibling origins are the one exception, and only for an edge: `amountOrigin`
#   on a nameplate amount and `quantumOrigin` on a lump or window size, where the claim's holder
#   states the author in an element of its own.
#
# The schema cannot say it
#   A `Claim` is one type wherever it sits, so `BoundDerivation` and `NarrowingDerivation` admit the
#   members of every position at once, and a validator passes a patience whose edge is a fusion
#   sum. identities/roster.sqlc lists the cells, one per identity, position and element, and a
#   derivation at a claim that is no cell is the claim naming the wrong equation. The roster lists
#   no cell twice, so joining it keeps one row per derivation.
-- pm:Claim/pm:boundOrigin and pm:Claim/pm:narrowsWhen taking pm:derivation, against the identity that computes the claim.
SELECT r.rule, p.filing, p.layer, p.violates, p.detail
FROM      (
    :compose(checks/roster.sqlc)
) r
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT c.filing, c.layer,
           i.identity IS NULL AS violates,
           format('%s claim %s files its %s as the output of `%s`', c.owns, c.seq, c.element,
                  c.identity) AS detail
    FROM      (
        :compose(epistemics/claim_derivations.sqlc)
    ) c
    LEFT JOIN (
        :compose(identities/roster.sqlc)
    ) i
           ON i.identity = c.identity::text
          AND i.owns     = c.owns
          AND i.element  = c.element
) p ON true
WHERE r.slug = 'identity_does_not_compute_the_claim'
